  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b><color=#FBBF24>THE IDEA</color></b>

    Processes (the blocks on the
    arena floor) wait in the <b>ready queue</b> for the one <b>CPU core</b>. The
    scheduler picks who runs next: FCFS, SRTF, Priority or Round Robin. The Gantt
    board shows the order and the waiting times.


    <b><color=#FBBF24>CONTROLS</color></b>

    Use
    a <b>workstation desk</b> to choose an algorithm, the <b>console</b> to run,
    step or reset, the <b>process editor</b> to change bursts, and the <b>challenge
    wall</b> for the quiz.

    <b>Desktop</b>  WASD walk, mouse look, <b>E</b> or
    click to use what the dot points at, <b>U</b> simulator window.

    <b>Phone</b> 
    thumbstick to walk, drag to look, tap to use.

    <b>Headset</b>  point and
    pull the trigger (or pinch) to use. <b>A</b> run / pause, <b>B</b> step, <b>X</b>
    simulator window.

    <b>Headset</b>  left stick walk, right stick turn (push
    up to teleport). Look at a controller to see its buttons.

    <b>Hands</b> 
    point + pinch to select; pinch the ground and release to teleport; pinch + flick
    sideways to turn; left palm up for MENU.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
